      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T19:55:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of this logic is now reliant on what DEFAULT_LOCK_STATE is when the image is compiled. I\u0027m not sure I think that\u0027s a good idea. We should be very explicit the settings we\u0027re assigning.",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_dc9edcf1",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T19:55:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like where you had 3 states before. We should probably use 2 bits. One for \"use next bit\u0027s value\" if 1, and use default compilation value if 0.\n\n#define BOARD_CONSOLE_LOCK_MODIFIED (1 \u003c\u003c 7)\n#define BOARD_CONSOLE_LOCK_UNLOCKED (0 \u003c\u003c 8)\n#define BOARD_CONSOLE_LOCK_LOCKED   (1 \u003c\u003c 8)\n\nLet\u0027s see what Vadim thinks.",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_bc9120a4",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T20:12:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is BOARD_CONSOLE_LOCK_MODIFIED supposed to do?",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_dc9edcf1",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_3f8ee2c1",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:25:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It says to use the value in bit 8 for console lock. On reset (non suspend wake) we\u0027d clear both bits, 7 and 8. You could use one bit, but I liked your original code where there was a notion of \"use this value\". You could get away with 1 bit if you make it such that it\u0027s the unlock bit. And we clear it at the right place. \n\nMy concern still is handling resume where we fallback. That fallback mechanism makes me uneasy about it picking up state saved by a previous image. I feel like we should have a version number stashed away in one of these fields where we invalidate then re-setup all these bits when the version number is different.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_bc9120a4",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_bc0e801b",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:30:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think one bit should be enough to indicate that console is unlocked.\n\nset when console is unlocked, cleared when the console is locked or if it is a restart for any other reason than resume from slleep.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_dc9edcf1",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_bf3f52ca",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:39:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Separate from this particular CL I\u0027m still concerned about deep sleep wake into a rolled back image. I\u0027d feel a lot more comfortable if we handled that situation explicitly by resetting bits like this unlock bit so that defaults are restored.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_bc0e801b",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_ff8b8a71",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:43:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, this is a good concern. How about we add locking the console unconditionally if a fallback situation is detected?\n\nThis way we still keep just one bit and act on it  and don\u0027 rewrite it all the time.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_bf3f52ca",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_5fb8fec5",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1136059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T21:59:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could check that the retry counter is the same as when we stored the lock state.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_ff8b8a71",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_72b971a8",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T22:09:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "you mean we would save the console state and the counter value? What would be the benefit?\n\nWe are not supposed to be falling back ever. If we ever do - lock the console and let the user unlock it. Keep it simple, less chance for doing something wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_5fb8fec5",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_15990708",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002124
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T23:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e yes, this is a good concern. How about we add locking the console\n \u003e unconditionally if a fallback situation is detected?\n \u003e \n \u003e This way we still keep just one bit and act on it  and don\u0027 rewrite\n \u003e it all the time.\n\nThat\u0027s what I described regarding keeping version number. I\u0027m not sure how fallback detection would be implemented. Sounds like an RO change? If so, I understand. Regardless, on that condition ensuring console is locked on that condition is what we need.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_ff8b8a71",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "da6cabba_552a9f91",
        "filename": "include/system.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 492,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-12-16T23:29:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fallback condition is detected by the RW, when it determines at run time that it is older than the other option present in the flash, in chip/g/system.c:system_process_retry_counter().\n\nRight now this invoked only when the AP sends the ReadPCR command, which might not happen right away.\n\nSo, I suggest to add the check (without looking at the counter) early in board_init and if fallback is detected - make sure the bit is cleared and console is locked before console is actually active.",
      "parentUuid": "da6cabba_15990708",
      "revId": "d9353c75fae6aa0300192b47e72d2db659773503",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
